ℹ Repeated publication phase reports cannot postpone a genuinely stalled upload
ℹ Oncall’s scheduled pass saves its private settings with its plan; a Save from the form opened before asks for none and changes nothing
ℹ An owner’s first Oncall Save that lands while the pass generates its own plan is the saved configuration
ℹ An Oncall plan saved before its owner token was made is the service’s to finish, never the owner’s
ℹ A genuinely owner-supplied credential stays needs_owner until the write-only door has it
ℹ A 2613-file catalogue source copies hands-off through a push timeout and a GitHub rate limit, resuming its staged pushes and completing a landed push by comparison
ℹ A paid Business preserves its coverage while standalone apps open their own checkout
ℹ One plan approval sets up Spool, Uptime and Lamp under one Business subscription, accepting only each approved first release
ℹ Business secrets are write-only, and the new doors refuse device, task and cross-origin credentials
ℹ A self-hosted Business gets an answers file, exact commands, a health check at its own address and a self-attested claim
ℹ A replaced or removed Business mail key reaches each app’s stored settings, Claim completes only for the Business owner, and a live app that stops answering needs attention again, but never for one lost probe
ℹ The scheduled pass takes every Business in turn, owner-waiting ones after those that can move
ℹ An unproved Managed Business can resume an older setup graph and claim Set up without bypassing its health check
